course: dictionary
lesson: 14760
title: Propriety: doing the right thing
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Propriety means behaving in a correct, polite way that follows the rules of good manners. It is a formal word, so you will meet it in old books, history and grown-up news. «Mrs Hale taught the girls the rules of propriety: sit up straight, speak softly and always say thank you.» The clues are sit up straight, speak softly and say thank you. These are all good manners, so propriety means correct, polite behaviour.
explain: The proprieties, with an s, means the rules of polite behaviour in society. «The butler bowed and kept to the proprieties all evening.» The clue is all evening: he followed the rules of manners the whole time.
explain: Adults also use propriety for honest, correct behaviour at work. «The judge questioned the propriety of the decision, because it seemed unfair.» The clues are questioned and unfair: people were asking whether the decision was right. Check your meaning by swapping it in. Does "questioned the correctness of the decision" still make sense? If so, you have it.
fact: Propriety means correct, polite and proper behaviour, following the rules of good manners.
fact: The proprieties means the rules of polite behaviour in society.
fact: In old novels, propriety was very important, especially for girls and women, who were told what was "proper".
fact: In adult life, propriety can mean acting honestly and correctly at work or in public office.
fact: Useful phrases: «a sense of propriety», «with propriety», «question the propriety of». Propriety is uncountable, so you do not say "a propriety".
exercise: «Mrs Hale taught the girls the rules of propriety.» What does propriety mean here? | *Correct, polite behaviour that follows good manners | Running fast in the rain | Loud singing and dancing
exercise: «The judge questioned the propriety of the decision.» What does this suggest? | People forgot about the decision completely | People were sure the decision was perfect | People wanted a bigger decision | *People wondered if the decision was fair and correct
exercise: Mia says, «She behaved with propriety at the dinner.» What does "with propriety" mean? | Quickly and carelessly | Angrily and loudly | *Politely and correctly
test: «The butler bowed and kept to the proprieties all evening.» What are the proprieties? | Stories about kings | The silver plates and cups | Old dances from long ago | *The rules of polite behaviour in society
test: Which word is closest in meaning to propriety? | Hurry | Anger | *Good manners | Rudeness
exam: «Amira had a sense of propriety, so she always waited her turn and said sorry.» What does "a sense of propriety" suggest about Amira? | She cannot tell right from wrong | She likes shouting in class | She is always late for school | *She knows what is correct and polite
